#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Solution.rst:37
msgid "Vertical Orifice Equation"
msgstr "Ecuación del orificio vertical"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Solution.rst:39
msgid ""
"**1)** Find the *vena contracta* (VC) coefficient ratio for an orifice in "
"the expert_inputs and print the result in a sentence. Please display 2 "
"significant figures."
msgstr ""
"**1)** Encuentra la razón de coeficientes *vena contracta* (VC) para un "
"orificio en el expert_inputs e imprime el resultado en una oración. Por "
"favor, muestra 2 cifras significativas."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Solution.rst:41
msgid ""
"`vena contracta calculation <https://colab.research.google.com/drive/1fWZQ-"
"BsXeINM31NgzbJO2Piv7NZug0cI#scrollTo=CZ5G4LzBRz6y&line=1&uniqifier=1>`_"
msgstr ""
"`cálculo de vena contracta <https://colab.research.google.com/drive/1fWZQ-"
"BsXeINM31NgzbJO2Piv7NZug0cI#scrollTo=CZ5G4LzBRz6y&line=1&uniqifier=1>`_"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Solution.rst:43
msgid "The *vena contracta* coefficient for an orifice is 0.63."
msgstr "El coeficiente de *vena contracta* para un orificio es 0,63."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Solution.rst:45
msgid ""
"**2)** The simple orifice Equation :math:`Q = {\\Pi _{vc}}{A_{or}}\\sqrt "
"{2g\\Delta h}` that we normally use is not applicable for vertically "
"oriented orifices that are partially or barely submerged. The `USGS "
"published a great solution "
"<https://il.water.usgs.gov/proj/feq/fequtl98.i2h/4_7aupdate.html>`__ for "
"flow through partially submerged vertically oriented orifices. AguaClara "
"uses a general solution for a vertically oriented orifice, which is "
"available in the physchem file as ``pc.flow_orifice_vert``. That function "
"handles vertically oriented orifices even if they are only partially "
"submerged."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Solution.rst:47
msgid ""
"The vertical orifice equation is based on the concept that the velocity "
"through the orifice at any point is equal to :math:`\\sqrt{2gh}`, where h is"
" the local depth of submergence. The total flow can be obtained by "
"integration of that velocity over the submerged area of the orifice."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Solution.rst:49
msgid ""
"For this question, you will create a well formatted graph with two curves to"
" display flow rate through a 5 cm diameter orifice oriented **vertically and"
" horizontally**."
msgstr ""
"Para esta pregunta, crearás un gráfico bien formateado con dos curvas para "
"mostrar caudal a través de un orificio de 5 cm de diámetro orientado "
"**vertical y horizontal**."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Solution.rst:51
msgid ""
"We want to be able to describe the height of the water in the orifice as "
"relative to the orifice diameter size. The relationship between velocity and"
" orifice diameter is true for orifices of any size, so it is valuable to "
"create a nondimensional model that can be understood for all diameters. The "
"flow rate that you will use for this question is as a function of the "
"normalized depth of water from 1 diameter below the center of the orifice to"
" 2 diameters above the center of the orifice."
msgstr ""
"Queremos poder describir la altura del agua en el orificio en relación con "
"el tamaño del diámetro del orificio. La relación entre velocidad y diámetro "
"del orificio es cierta para orificios de cualquier tamaño, por lo que es "
"valioso crear un modelo no dimensional que pueda entenderse para todos los "
"diámetros. El caudal que usarás para esta pregunta es una función de la "
"profundidad normalizada del agua desde 1 diámetro por debajo del centro del "
"orificio hasta 2 diámetros por encima del centro del orificio."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Solution.rst:53
msgid "The steps for making the graph are as follows:"
msgstr "Los pasos para hacer el gráfico son los siguientes:"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Solution.rst:55
msgid ""
"Use ``np.linspace`` to generate an array of 100 dimensionless water surface "
"elevations. The surface elevations should be normalized (also referred to as"
" nondimensionalized) by the diameter of the orifice, and should range from "
"-1 to 2 orifice diameters."
msgstr ""
"Utiliza ``np.linspace`` para generar un conjunto de 100 elevaciones "
"adimensionales de la superficie del agua. Las elevaciones superficiales "
"deben normalizarse (también denominadas no dimensionalizadas) por el "
"diámetro del orificio, y deben variar de -1 a 2 diámetros de orificio."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Solution.rst:56
msgid ""
"Create a second array for water elevation (with units) by multiplying the "
"normalized water elevation array by the orifice diameter."
msgstr ""
"Crear un segundo arreglo para la elevación del agua (con unidades) "
"multiplicando el conjunto normalizado de elevación del agua por el diámetro "
"del orificio."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Solution.rst:57
msgid ""
"Create two arrays of flow rates through the orifice: one for the horizontal "
"orifice orientation and one for the vertical orifice orientation. Use the "
"two orifice equations ``pc.flow_orifice`` and ``pc.flow_orifice_vert`` in "
"the physchem file, with orifice diameter and the dimensional water elevation"
" array you created as inputs."
msgstr ""
"Crea dos matrices de caudales a través del orificio: uno para la orientación"
" horizontal del orificio y otro para la orientación vertical. Utiliza las "
"dos ecuaciones de orificio ``pc.flow_orifice`` y ``pc.flow_orifice_vert`` en"
" el archivo de physchem, con el diámetro del orificio y el array dimensional"
" de elevación del agua que creaste como entradas."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Solution.rst:58
msgid ""
"Plot the curves for vertical and horizontal orifice flow in L/s as a "
"function of the normalized height of water."
msgstr ""
"Grafica las curvas para el flujo vertical y horizontal de orificios en L/s "
"en función de la altura normalizada del agua."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Solution.rst:59
msgid ""
"Label the graph with flow rate in L/s as the y-axis and with normalized "
"water elevation above the center of the orifice as the x-axis."
msgstr ""
"Etiqueta el gráfico con caudal en L/s como eje y y con la elevación "
"normalizada del agua por encima del centro del orificio como eje x."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Solution.rst:60
msgid "Include a legend for the two curves."
msgstr "Incluye una leyenda para las dos curvas."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Solution.rst:62
msgid ""
"`Colab worksheet comparing vertical and horizontal orifice flow "
"<https://colab.research.google.com/drive/1fWZQ-"
"BsXeINM31NgzbJO2Piv7NZug0cI#scrollTo=F7l7sG0aR24k&line=4&uniqifier=1>`_"
msgstr ""
"`hoja de cálculo de Colab que compara el flujo de orificios vertical y "
"horizontal <https://colab.research.google.com/drive/1fWZQ-"
"BsXeINM31NgzbJO2Piv7NZug0cI#scrollTo=F7l7sG0aR24k&line=4&uniqifier=1>`_"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Solution.rst:71
msgid "Horizontal vs. Vertical Orifice Orientation"
msgstr "Orientación horizontal vs. vertical del orificio"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Solution.rst:73
msgid ""
"**3)** Write a paragraph about what the graph means by explaining the "
"following two items: - Explain why the vertical orifice equation predicts "
"more flow when the water level is below the center of the orifice and "
"predicts less flow when the water level is above the center of the orifice. "
"It might help to draw a picture of what the equations are describing to "
"understand what is happening here! - Explain how the horizontal orifice "
"equation function from ``physchem.py`` predicts the flow rate for "
"submergence depths that are negative. You will need to find the function and"
" look at the code."
msgstr ""
"**3)** Escribe un párrafo sobre lo que significa el gráfico explicando los "
"siguientes dos elementos: - Explica por qué la ecuación del orificio "
"vertical predice más flujo cuando el nivel del agua está por debajo del "
"centro del orificio y predice menos flujo cuando el nivel del agua está por "
"encima del centro del orificio. ¡Puede ayudar dibujar una imagen de lo que "
"describen las ecuaciones para entender lo que está ocurriendo aquí! - "
"Explica cómo la función de ecuación del orificio horizontal de "
"``physchem.py`` predice el caudal para profundidades de sumergencia que son "
"negativas. Tendrás que encontrar la función y mirar el código."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Solution.rst:76
msgid "Explanation"
msgstr "Explicación"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Solution.rst:78
msgid ""
"The vertical orifice has the lower part of the orifice partially submerged "
"before the horizontal orifice has any part submerged. This explains why the "
"vertical orifice has more flow than the horizontal orifice between -0.5 and "
"0."
msgstr ""
"El orificio vertical tiene la parte inferior parcialmente sumergida antes de"
" que el orificio horizontal tenga alguna parte sumergida. Esto explica por "
"qué el orificio vertical tiene más flujo que el orificio horizontal entre "
"-0,5 y 0."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Solution.rst:80
msgid ""
"The horizontal orifice has higher flow rates between 0 and 0.5 because it is"
" fully submerged when the vertical orifice is still not fully submerged."
msgstr ""
"El orificio horizontal tiene caudales más altos entre 0 y 0,5 porque está "
"completamente sumergido cuando el orificio vertical aún no está "
"completamente sumergido."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Solution.rst:82
msgid ""
"At the elevation where the vertical orifice is first fully submerged the "
"flow rate through the vertical orifice is less than the flow rate through "
"the horizontal orifice. This is a result of the nonlinear relationships "
"between depth of submergence and velocity."
msgstr ""
"A la elevación en la que el orificio vertical está completamente sumergido "
"por primera vez, la caudal a través del orificio vertical es menor que la "
"caudal a través del orificio horizontal. Esto es resultado de las relaciones"
" no lineales entre la profundidad de sumergimiento y la velocidad."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Solution.rst:84
msgid ""
"The difference between the two equations becomes negligible for submergence "
"greater than 1 diameter."
msgstr ""
"La diferencia entre ambas ecuaciones se vuelve insignificante para "
"sumergencias mayores a 1 de diámetro."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Solution.rst:86
msgid ""
"For negative depths of submergence the horizontal orifice function uses an "
"if statement to set the flow rate through the orifice equal to zero."
msgstr ""
"Para profundidades negativas de sumergencia, la función de orificio "
"horizontal utiliza una sentencia if para colocar el caudal a través del "
"orificio igual a cero."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Solution.rst:89
msgid "Linear Flow Orifice Meter (LFOM)"
msgstr "Medidor de orificio de flujo lineal (LFOM)"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Solution.rst:91
msgid ""
"A linear flow orifice meter is used in AguaClara plants to measure the plant"
" flow rate and to provide a linear relationship between flow rate and the "
"depth of water in the entrance tank. Below, we use the LFOM code to obtain a"
" design for a linear flow orifice meter. Your task will be to test this "
"design using the orifice equations to see if it is correct. We have a custom"
" `LFOM class <https://aguaclara.github.io/aguaclara/design/lfom.html>`_ that"
" defines the LFOM properties. This code will be updated soon based on the "
"code below. In the meantime, the code below can be used for calculations."
msgstr ""
"En las plantas de AguaClara se utiliza un medidor de orificio de flujo "
"lineal para medir el caudal de la planta y para proporcionar una relación "
"lineal entre caudal y la profundidad del agua en el tanque de entrada. A "
"continuación, usamos el código LFOM para obtener un diseño de un medidor de "
"orificio de flujo lineal. Tu tarea será probar este diseño usando las "
"ecuaciones del orificio para ver si es correcto. Disponemos de una clase "
"personalizada `LFOM "
"<https://aguaclara.github.io/aguaclara/design/lfom.html>`_ que define las "
"propiedades del LFOM. Este código se actualizará pronto en función del "
"código que aparece a continuación. Mientras tanto, el código siguiente puede"
" utilizarse para cálculos."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Solution.rst:93
msgid ""
"The following questions are all answered in one big block of code to make it"
" easy to change values and then see the resulting graph."
msgstr ""
"Las siguientes preguntas se responden en un gran bloque de código para "
"facilitar el cambio de valores y luego ver el gráfico resultante."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Solution.rst:95
msgid ""
"**4)** Create a function that calculates the flow rate through the LFOM as a"
" function of only water elevation using the vertical orifice function. Use "
"the arrays for LFOM key parameters, given above as "
"``my_LFOM.orifice_diameter``, ``my_LFOM.n_orifices_per_row``, and "
"``my_LFOM.height_orifices``."
msgstr ""
"**4)** Crea una función que calcule el caudal a través del LFOM solo en "
"función de la elevación del agua usando la función de orificio vertical. "
"Utiliza los arrays para los parámetros clave del LFOM, indicados arriba como"
" ``my_LFOM.orifice_diameter``, ``my_LFOM.n_orifices_per_row``, y "
"``my_LFOM.height_orifices``."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Solution.rst:97
msgid ""
"Create an array for depth of submergence for each row of orifices at a given"
" a height of water in the LFOM. This array is dependent on the water "
"elevation (which should be your function input) and the height of the LFOM "
"orifices (which is from the LFOM key parameters). Use this submergence depth"
" array as the “height” input to your vertical orifice function. The array "
"should be created within your function."
msgstr ""
"Crea un array para la profundidad de sumergimiento de cada fila de orificios"
" a una altura dada del agua en el LFOM. Este array depende de la elevación "
"del agua (que debería ser tu función de entrada) y de la altura de los "
"orificios del LFOM (que proviene de los parámetros clave del LFOM). Usa este"
" array de profundidad de sumergencia como la entrada de \"altura\" para tu "
"función de orificio vertical. El array debe crearse dentro de tu función."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Solution.rst:99
msgid ""
"To calculate the flow rate through the LFOM, multiply the calculated flow "
"for each row of orifices by the number of orifices in that row "
"(``my_LFOM.n_orifices_per_row``) to get an array of flows through each row "
"of orifices. Note: the vertical orifice function will report zero flow for "
"any orifices that aren’t submerged, so you can send the whole array of depth"
" of submergence for each row of orifices."
msgstr ""
"Para calcular la caudal a través del LFOM, multiplica el flujo calculado "
"para cada fila de orificios por el número de orificios en esa fila "
"(``my_LFOM.n_orifices_per_row``) para obtener un array de flujos a través de"
" cada fila de orificios. Nota: la función de orificio vertical informará de "
"flujo cero para cualquier orificio que no esté sumergido, por lo que puedes "
"enviar todo el array de profundidad de sumersión para cada fila de "
"orificios."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Solution.rst:101
msgid ""
"At the end of your function, sum flows from each row of the LFOM and return "
"that value with the correct units."
msgstr ""
"Al final de tu función, la suma fluye de cada fila del LFOM y devuelve ese "
"valor con las unidades correctas."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Solution.rst:103
msgid ""
"Add a comment under the function definition to explain what the function "
"does (see any of the aguaclara design files for examples of descriptive "
"comments)."
msgstr ""
"Añade un comentario bajo la definición de función para explicar qué hace la "
"función (consulta cualquiera de los archivos de diseño de aguaclara para "
"ejemplos de comentarios descriptivos)."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Solution.rst:105
msgid ""
"**5)** Calculate the total flow through the LFOM using the vertical orifice "
"equation for the case when the water level is at the maximum water level for"
" the LFOM, ``HeadlossLfom``. You are checking to make sure that the LFOM "
"produces the correct target flow (given as ``Flow``) at the maximum height. "
"Does it?"
msgstr ""
"**5)** Calcula el caudal total a través del LFOM usando la ecuación del "
"orificio vertical para el caso en que el nivel del agua esté en el nivel del"
" agua máximo para el LFOM, ``HeadlossLfom``. Estás comprobando que el LFOM "
"produce el flujo objetivo correcto (dado como ``Flow``) a la altura máxima. "
"¿Lo hace?"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Solution.rst:110
msgid ""
"**6)** We want to compare the actual flow rate through the LFOM to the "
"expected flow rate through the elevation as a function of water depth. "
"Create a graph of the normalized actual and expected flow rates, using the "
"following steps:"
msgstr ""
"**6)** Queremos comparar la caudal real a través del LFOM con la caudal "
"esperada a través de la elevación en función de la profundidad del agua. "
"Crea un gráfico de los caudales reales y esperados normalizados, usando los "
"siguientes pasos:"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Solution.rst:112
msgid ""
"Create an 100-unit long array of water depths using ``np.linspace``. Note: "
"the expected flow rate at elevation zero is zero, which makes the normalized"
" flow rate undefined for zero elevation. An undefined normalized flow will "
"not run and Python will report an error. You can solve this by beginning "
"your water depth array at a very small (nonzero) elevation. You can end your"
" water depth array at the maximum water depth. Recall that an array of "
"elevations should have units of length."
msgstr ""
"Crea un array de profundidades de agua de 100 unidades usando "
"``np.linspace``. Nota: el caudal esperado en elevación cero es cero, lo que "
"hace que el caudal normalizado sea indefinido para elevación cero. Un flujo "
"normalizado indefinido no se ejecutará y Python reportará un error. Puedes "
"solucionar esto comenzando tu array de profundidad de agua en una elevación "
"muy pequeña (distinta de cero). Puedes terminar tu array de profundidad de "
"agua en la profundidad máxima del agua. Recuerda que un array de elevaciones"
" debe tener unidades de longitud."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Solution.rst:113
msgid ""
"Create an array of normalized actual flow rates at each water depth; use the"
" function you created in Problem 4 and a ``for`` loop (the function you "
"created in Problem 4 probably can’t handle an array of depths as input, so "
"you need the ``for`` loop to cycle through each depth value to make your "
"array of flows)."
msgstr ""
"Crea un array de caudales reales normalizados en cada profundidad de agua; "
"usa la función que creaste en el Problema 4 y un bucle de ``for`` (la "
